## 5. Remote Control Media Keys & Spatial D-Pad Routing

### 5.1 webOS Dedicated Media Keys
When playback is active, the remote media keys trigger:
| Key | Keycode | Action | Execution Path |
|---|---|---|---|
| Play | 415 | `MEDIA_PLAY` | `PlayerController.play()`, `PlayerOSDController.resetIdleTimer()` |
| Pause | 19 | `MEDIA_PAUSE` | `PlayerController.pause()`, `PlayerOSDController.showHUD()` |
| Play/Pause | 179 | `MEDIA_PLAY_PAUSE` | `PlayerController.togglePlayPause()` |
| Stop | 413 / 178 | `MEDIA_STOP` | `CinejoyApp.exitPlayer()` (initiates 5-stage teardown, switches to details) |
| FastForward | 417 / 228 | `MEDIA_FAST_FORWARD` | `PlayerController.seek(10)`, `showSeekFeedback(true, 10)` |
| Rewind | 412 / 227 | `MEDIA_REWIND` | `PlayerController.seek(-10)`, `showSeekFeedback(false, 10)` |
| Back | 461 / 27 | `BACK` | Hierarchical: closes modal if open; otherwise `CinejoyApp.exitPlayer()` |

### 5.2 Spatial D-Pad Navigation Graph
- **HUD Visible State**:
  - `data-nav-tier="top"`: `#player-back-btn`
  - `data-nav-tier="scrubber"`: `#osd-scrubber` (role="slider")
  - `data-nav-tier="actions"`: `#osd-rewind-btn` -> `#osd-play-btn` -> `#osd-forward-btn` -> `#osd-subtitles-btn` -> `#osd-server-btn`
  - When `#osd-scrubber` is focused, `ArrowLeft` / `ArrowRight` adjusts seek head without losing focus.
- **HUD Hidden State (`.osd-hidden`)**:
  - `ArrowLeft`: Seeks backward (-10s), displays seek feedback toast, wakes HUD (`showHUD()`).
  - `ArrowRight`: Seeks forward (+10s), displays seek feedback toast, wakes HUD (`showHUD()`).
  - `ArrowUp` / `ArrowDown`: Wakes HUD (`showHUD()`), sets spatial focus directly to `#osd-play-btn`.
  - `Enter` / `OK` (13): Wakes HUD (`showHUD()`), toggles play/pause.

### 5.3 OSD Auto-Hide Timer Lifecycle
- The OSD automatically hides after **4000ms** of user inactivity while video is actively PLAYING.
- **Permanent Inactivity Suspension**:
  - The auto-hide timer is canceled and permanently suspended while the video is PAUSED (asserted in `app/test-m5.js` S3.3 and `adversarial-m5-osd-remote.js` ADV-S4.3).
  - The timer is canceled and suspended while any modal dialog (Subtitles, Server, Error) is active (`_activeModal !== null`).
- **Activity Reset**:
  - Any remote keypress, mouse movement, or seek command calls `resetIdleTimer()`, resetting the 4000ms countdown.
  - Race condition immunity: Keystrokes arriving at the 3950ms–4050ms boundary reset the timer without premature HUD hiding (`ADV-S4.1`, `ADV-S4.2`).

